&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI KARHA SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt; is situated in the Karah Village, Tehsil Pehowa and Distt Kurukshetra. &lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; came here during his first udasi via Kurukshetra and Pehowa. Here lived a Pandit who was very proudy for his his Knowledge. GURU SAHIB showed him right way to the life. &lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/strong&gt; came here while going to SHRI NANAK MATA SAHIB, When Baba Almast ji informed him that Gorakh Sadhu&#39;s have captured GURUDWARA SHRI NANAK MATA SAHIB and renamed it as Gorakh Mata. Here lived a man named Kalu a blind and physical Handicapped, who used to worship GURU SAHIB a lot. When kalu came to know that GURU SAHIB had come, He reached GURU SAHIB crawling and said GURU JI please cure me from this disease. A Sikh sitting near GURU SAHIB asked Kalu to touch GURU SAHIB&#39;s horse feets dust with his eyes. He did as said and he was able to see everything. GURU SAHIB blessed with him and said him to work there. Keep the GURU KA LANGAR alive and don&#39;t go to any one for any type of Donation. Your diseases will be cured.&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU TEG BAHADUR SAHIB JI&lt;/strong&gt; came here. A Masand was living here appointed by
&lt;strong&gt; SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/strong&gt;, When he came to know about &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU TEGBAHADUR JI&lt;/strong&gt;&quot;s arrival, he afraid of Muslims didn&#39;t came to meet GURU SAHIB. A person served GURU SAHIB with great devotion. GURU SAHIB asked him not to use TAMBAKOO and blessed with with GOD&#39;s wishes every thing will be blessed to you. And also Gave him 500 rs for Digging well and Garden at that place. But he instead of getting garden and well on GURU GHAR&#39;s name did all things on his name. &lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/strong&gt; came to this place while going Siana Sayyada and stopped under IMLI TREE. GURU SAHIB also warned masand appointed by &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU TEGBAHADUR JI &lt;/strong&gt;for his act. That tree is still preserved here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI TEESRI, SATVIN &amp;amp; ATHVIN PATSHAHI SAHIB &lt;/strong&gt; is situated in the Kurukshetra City.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDASS JI&lt;/strong&gt;: In 1523 &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDASS JI &lt;/strong&gt;came to this sacred place with his family on solar eclipse. From the time of Babar, there was tax on pilgrimage for hindu pilgrims. So GURU SAHIB stayed outside the city and denied giving paying tax to Mughal Rulers. When this news reached to Akbar, he ordered not to take tax from &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMAR DAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; and his sikhs. The whole congregation bowed to GURU SAHIB and they first time took holy bath without paying any tax.&lt;/p&gt;

&quot;Bhai Ham Karah Kiaa, Kis pas mangah sabh bhag satguru pichey payi || &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HAR RAI JI&lt;/strong&gt;: On 10th March 1656, on Amavas night, &lt;B/&gt;SHRI GURU HAR RAI JI &lt;/B&gt;came to this place and preached the sikh sangat.

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HAR KRISHAN JI&lt;/strong&gt;: When Ram Rai came to know the Gurgaddi has been passed on to his younger Brother SHRI GURU HARKARISHAN SAHIB JI, he took the help of Mughal darbar to take illegal possession over GUR GADDI. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARKRISHAN JI&lt;/strong&gt; was called to Delhi by Aurangzeb to weaken the sikhi spirit. But &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARKRISHAN JI&lt;/strong&gt; denied his invitation caring the quote of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARRAI JI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; (&quot;Na Malech ko darshan deo&quot;),&lt;BR/&gt;
but after request from Raja Jai Singh Rajasthan and sangat he went there. From Kiratpur Sahib via Panjokhrha he reached to kurukshetra, and pay obsession on his father&#39;s place and stayed in the house of Tarkhan) where &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMAR DAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARRAI JI&lt;/strong&gt; stayed. In the remembrance of his father &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARKRISHAN JI&lt;/strong&gt; organized a Langar, where different varieties were prepared and all the sangat took meal in pangat.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt; &lt;B&gt;GURDWARA SRI JANAM ASTHAAN PIR BUDU SHAH JI&lt;/B&gt; is situated in the Sadhora Village in Yamuna Nagar Distt. Haryana. Peer ji was an admirer of &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt;. This place is birth place of Peer Budhu shah ji. Peer Budhu Shah Ji got great respect in Sikh History as well as with &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt;. Once 500 Soldiers from Aurangezeb&#39;s army got fired and came to see Peer Budhu Shah jI at Sadhora(because they were shias Muslims) and it was ordered that no one should employ them in any army. They requested peer Buddhu Shah that they are disable now as they have sold all their belongings for the sake of food and the situation is that now they have to sell their weapons too to survive. &lt;/P&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt; 				They wanted to enter in army of such a man who was not scared of Aurangzeb. Peer Buddhu Shah took the pathans to &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; and asked GURU SAHIB to engage them in his army. At his recommendation, the GURU SAHIB engaged 500 Pathan soldiers under the command of four leaders, Kale Khan, Bhikham Khan, Nijabat Khan and Hayat Khan(Omar khan). They were all trained by GURU SAHIB. Soon, there was a battle between GURU SAHIB and Hill Rulers who started the battle as they were scared by the gathering strength of the GURU SAHIB community and the bold activities of GURU SAHIB. With this the pathans who had been recommended by Pir ji into the GURU SAHIB&#39;s army started to move away from the GURU SAHIB&#39;s force. They were leaving the army giving various excuses. GURU SAHIB did not pressurised them and said they could leave and go if this is what they wanted. One Pathan, Kale Khan did not leave GURU SAHIB. &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; wrote a letter to Peer ji to bring to his attention the fact that the pathans recommended by him and who had been drawing salaries from the GURU SAHIB&#39;s darbar were now betraying the cause when need there was a serious need. When Pir Budhu Shah came to know this disloyalty of the Pathans, he came to the GURU SAHIB&#39;s aid with his seven hundred followers, four sons and two brothers. GURU SAHIB was very much happy to see his followers fighting against hill chiefs as they were not professionally soldiers. GURU SAHIB felt very happy seeing the devotion of peer Buddhu Shah. Many of the Pir&#39;s disciples as well as two of his sons, Ashraf and Muhammad Shah, and his brother, Bhure Shah fell in the action. &lt;/P&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt; 				After the battle &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; offered rich presents to the Pir which he politely declined to accept. However he, as the tradition goes, begged the GURU SAHIB to bestow upon him the comb from his hair and the turban he was going to tie. The GURU SAHIB gave him the two articles and a small kirpan(sword)&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;On 21 March 1704 Usman Khan torutured and killed Peer Budhu Shah Ji. Sri Guru Gobind Singh ji came here four times.&lt;/P&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI KAPAL MOCHAN SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt; is situated in the Village Bilaspur (Kapal Mochan) in Yamuna nagar Distt. Its 17 KM from Jagadhari Town. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; reached this place from Haridwar via Saharanpur in the year 1584 Bikrami on Katakk&#39;s full moon while blessing the people. During GURU SAHIB&#39;s journey, a merchant offered food to all the saints. When everyone sat in queues, a child took birth at the merchant&#39;s house listening to which the saints stopped eating food due to Sootak (a period of 13 to 40 days after childbirth). &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; then said:&lt;/p&gt;

Salok Mahalla 1 ||Je Kar Sootak Manniye Sab Te Sootak Hoye |&lt;BR&gt; Gohe Te Lakdi Andar Keeda Hoye ||&lt;BR&gt; Jaite Daane Ann Ke Jeeya Baajh Naa Koye |&lt;BR&gt; Pehla Paani Jeev Hai Jit Hariya Sab Koye ||&lt;BR&gt; Sootak Kiyo Kar Rakhiye Sootak Paveh Rasoye | &lt;BR&gt; Nanak Sootak Ev Na Uttarye Gyaan Uttarye Dhoye || 1 ||

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Listening to this shabad, the Saints &amp;amp; the Pandits fell into Guru Ji&#39;s feet &amp;amp; became Guru Ji&#39;s Sikhs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;In the year 1746, &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/strong&gt;, after winning the battle of Bhangani, came to this place &amp;amp; took rest for 52 days. The people who used to show disrespect to the Sarovars, Guru Sahib got their turbans taken off, tore them &amp;amp; offered robe of honor (Siropas) to the Singhs. At this place, &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/strong&gt; gave a Hukamnama to the Pandits which is placed with the Pandits till date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The Birth Anniversary of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; on Katakk&#39;s full moon is celebrated with great joy &amp;amp; enthusiasm. The followers come from far off places to visit the place &amp;amp; get their wish fulfilled by taking a dip in holy water of the Sarovar.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI PATSHAHI NAUVIN SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt; is situated in village Sekha, Distt Barnala. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU TEGBAHADUR SAHIB JI&lt;/strong&gt; came here while on Malwa tour. GURU SAHIB rested here on bank of water reservoir. GURU SAHIB himself took bath in it and blessed who so ever will take bath in his/her wishes will come true. Here lived a person named Chaudary Tirloka Jawanda. He was head of this area and very proudy man. This area was of Jawanda&#39;s and there were total 22 village of Jawanda&#39;s. Tirloka was follower of Mado Das Sadhu. When GURU SAHIB was sitting with sangat, Tirloka riding on horse passed by. Sangat told GURU SAHIB about Tirloka.&lt;/p&gt;&quot; &lt;b&gt;Sun bole Satgur ris bhoye | nahi bahia nahi tehia koi ||
&quot;kuch nahi rehar ujar Sub jaweh | bachuh ju aaprus gram basaweh ||
nahi sardari nahi sardar | mar mar janmeh hoye khuaar ||&lt;/b&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;When ladies from Tirloka Jawandas came to know about this she came to see GURU SAHIB. But GURU SAHIB had left by the time. She followed GURU SAHIB and met at village Kattu. She served GURU SAHIB and sangat woith milk. And requested GURU SAHIB to take back his wordings. GURU SAHIB asked them to set up there village at some far place from here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GURDWARA SRI DERA BABA NANAK SAHIB&lt;/b&gt; is situated in the Dera Baba Nanak city of District Gurdaspur.&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
 As its name defines its related to &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/b&gt;. GURU SAHIB came to meet his family, wife Sulakhani Ji, Son Baba Sri Chand Ji and Baba Lakhami Das Ji after first Udasi. They were had come to meet Mata Sulakhni Ji&#39;s father Lala Mulraaj, who was patwari (Revenue Officer) at Village Pakhoke Randhawa. When GURU SAHIB came here, he used to meditate on bank of well Ajita Randhawa da khooh. On the Stage situated in the Gurudwara Sahib, GURU SAHIB had discussion with Ajita Randhawa and later he became GURU SAHIBs follower. When &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&#39;s&lt;/b&gt; body was cremated at GURDWARA SRI DARBAR SAHIB KARTARPUR, PAKISTAN, The pot containing ashes of GURU SAHIB was also buried there. But some time later there was flood in Ravi river and it was approaching towards GUUDWARA SAHIB. Baba Sri Chand took the pot of ashes from there and buried it here at the place of Thara Sahibs. &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI&lt;/b&gt; came here and did kirtan at time of death of Baba Dharam Chand Ji (Grand Son of &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/b&gt;). This place was also visited by &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI, SRI GURU AMAR DAS JI&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt;. Later the golden guband (Dome) was made by Maharaj Ranjit Singh ji. Dera Baba Nanak being situated only 1 km from India Pakistan border, and GURDWARA SRI DARBAR SAHIB KARTARPUR, PAKISTAN is just 4 km from border. In 2019 Pakistan Govt opened a special corridor for Indian Sangat who go there and have darshan without any Visa requirement.&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;/BR&gt;Link for Booking Yatra for Indian Sangat going to Gurudwara Shri Darbar Sahib Kartarpur, Pakistan.  to  :- &lt;a href=&quot;https://prakashpurb550.mha.gov.in/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt; www.prakashpurb550.mha.gov.in&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI PATSHAHI DASVIN SAHIB, NANOWAL&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
This Gurudwara Sahib situated in village Nanowal, Teh Garshankar Distt Hoshairpur. &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; came here from Khera Kalmot. Here GURU SAHIB honored Bhai Sangat Sahib ji for his services. GURU SAHIB presented Bhai Sahib a Hukamnama Sahib. That Hukamnama Sahib is still preserved over here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI CHAUBARA SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt; is situated in Village Cheetanwala Teh Nabha Distt Patiala. This Village is situated on Nabha-Sangrur road and is also known as Mansurpur as it was under the rulling of Mansoor Ali Khan Rajput. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; came here at Bhai Chanan Mal Ji&#39;s residence. Bhai Sahib arranged GURU SAHIB to rest at Chaubara. Bhai Chanan Mal ji arranged Bhoj(free food) for all in respect of GURU SAHIB. And Bhai Sahib invited people from every cast for the Bhoj. At that time a son was born at the house of Bhai Sahib. Brahmans Left the place and said that your house is now sutak (impure, is not pure now because of birth). Listening to this GURU SAHIB uttered following Shabad which are listed in Shri Asa Di Var and &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU GRANTH SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt; also.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;

Jekar sutak manye sab tai sutak hoye|| &lt;br&gt;
gohe ate lakdi andar kida hoye||jete dane ann ke jia baaj n koye || &lt;br&gt;
pahila paani jio hai jit harya sab koye||sutak kuon kari rakhye sutak pave rasoyi|| &lt;br&gt;
nanak sutak eve na utrye gyaan utaare dhoye||1||&lt;br&gt;
man ka sutak lobh hai jivah sutak kurhu|| akhi sutak vekhna par tria par dhan rup||&lt;br&gt;
kani sutak kan pai laitbari khahi|| nanak hansa aadmibade jam puri jahi||&lt;br&gt;
sabo sutak bharam hai duja lage jaye|| jaman marna hukam hai bhane aave jaye||&lt;br&gt;
khana pina pavitra hai diton rizak sambhahi|| nanak jinhi gurmukh bujhya tinha sutak nahi||&lt;br&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Listening to this all the brahmins understood the meaning of Sutak and then every had food sitting in Pangat. GURU SAHIB also blessed that whoso ever here will have Langar in Pangat or will distribute langar, all his wishes will come true.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI THADA SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt; is situated in the Samana city Distt Patiala.
&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;
When &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU TEGBAHADUR SAHIB JI&lt;/strong&gt; started his journey towards Delhi, He came here via-Kiratpur Sahib, Bharatgarh Sahib, Ropar, Makar, Kabulpur, Bahadurgarh and Moti Baag. GURU SAHIB came here to the place of Sai Anayat Ali. Adjoining was the Area of Cruel Muslim, who had thrown Cow Bone in the well when GURU SAHIB&#39;s Sikh went there for water. After that GURU SAHIB got a well dug there. Bhikhan Shah owner of the near by Garhi was also great follower of GURU SAHIB, He offered lots of gift for GURU SAHIB. One day Nawab Bhikhan Shah met Muslim Soldiers who came here to arrest GURU SAHIB. On conversation Nawab Bhikhan Shah told them that Samana is place of Pure Muslim so SIKH GURU Cannot stay here. And later he himself came to GURU SAHIB and told him the whole story and requested to Accompany with him to Garhi. Nawab requested GURU SAHIB that it will be shame on his family that we got you arrested from our home. So from here onward GURU SAHIB left towards Nawab Bhikhan Shah&#39;s Garhi where GURUDWARA SHRI GARHI SAHIB is situated.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI ATAL JI SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt; is situated in the Distt City Amritsar. It is situated on the back side of &lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI HARIMANDIR SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt;. Baba Atal Rai was born in Samvat 1676 at Amritsar to &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/strong&gt;, From early age he was intelligent, lively and a deeply religious boy. He was called &quot;Baba&quot; because he carried a wise head over his young shoulders. He used to play with his age-mates and tell them many wise things. Whatever he said, even in jest, had some deep humane meaning. All his playmates loved and obeyed him. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI &lt;/strong&gt; was specially fond of him. He used to take him in his lap, cuddle him and say, “God has given you much power. Don’t make a show of it. If you have to use it, use it with caution and wisdom. Don’t waste it away on little things”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;One of Baba Atal’s playmates was Mohan, who was about the same age as Baba Atal. One day they played on until the night fell. At the end of day it was Mohan&#39;s turn. It was mutually agreed that Mohan will give his turn next morning, and they returned home. That night, mohan got bitten by a cobra. He screamed in agony. Next morning, all the boys reached the playground, except Mohan. Baba Atal Rai inquired about Mohan and came to know about the incident. Baba Atal Rai went straight to Mohan’s home. He found Mohan’s parents and others in deep mourning. When told that Mohan was dead, Baba Atal Rai said, “No, he can’t be dead. He is pretending to be dead. He does not wish to give me my turn. I will make him get up.” Saying this, he went to Mohan’s room. He touched him with his stick and said, “Mohan, get up and say ‘Satnam Waheguru’. Open your eyes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Upon this, Mohan got up as if from sleep. The news of Mohan’s revival spread like wild fire. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI
&lt;/strong&gt; also heard about what his son had done. He was not at all pleased. He said, We must obey God’s will. We should not try to undo what He has done.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;When Baba Atal Rai returned home, GURU SAHIB said to him &quot;You acted against GOD&#39;s will. Baba Atal Rai ji went away. He took his bath in the sacred sarovar, took four rounds of the sacred Harimandir Sahib and went to the nearby Kaulsar Sarovar (lake) - his favorite haunt. he laid down there, After that, he departed peacefully for his True Home on July 23, 1628 A.D.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/strong&gt; soon learned of his son’s passing away in these strange circumstances. He advised his family and his Sikhs not to go into mourning, saying:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;“All those who are born must die.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Such is the Almighty’s Will.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;What pleases Him is good.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;We should accept it cheerfully.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Atal’s name and fame shall live for ever.”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Baba Atal’s body was cremated at the spot where he had renounced it. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/strong&gt; said, “Atal has, by God’s Will, given up his body in his ninth year. A nine storied Memorial shall be built here, so that it can be seen from afar.”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Later, the tower was built between 1778 and 1784. At the spot now stands a beautiful nine storied GURUDWARA SAHIB known as Baba Atal Sahib. To express their reverence to his bountiful nature, people call out to the open hearted prince of truth:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;“O Baba Atal, Pakkian Pakaian ghal.”&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;i.e. O Baba, the revered one, send us well-baked bread to satiate our hunger. Since then, faithful Sikhs distribute cakes of bread to all visitors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/strong&gt; also blessed with following things&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your Place will be tallest in the city.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Who so ever will come to Amritsar, his trip will be fruitful if he visits your place.&lt;/li&gt;	&lt;li&gt;Sanagt will get their wishes fulfilled at your doorstep.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Needful will get food from your doorstep.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have been appointed the head of city, Who so ever will recite you at his end time, he will get your blessings.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI BHAI MANJ DA KHOOH&lt;/strong&gt; is situated in Sultanvind Distt. Amritsar  Bhai Manj Sahib Ji whose real name was  Tiratha , was a fore runner &amp;amp; preacher of this sultanate. He had Sakhi Sarvar Da Peerkhana  at his home. Tiratha used to visit &quot; Nigahe Sarvar Pir &quot; every year. He was the Chaudhary of the village. Chaudhary is the owner of the village. He was very rich &amp;amp; was a well known person. Bhai Manj Ji was a resident of village Kang Mai ( Distt. Hoshiarpur) &amp;amp; had two Peerkhana&#39;s  at his place. Every thursday he used to offer bread (rot) at the Peerkhana &amp;amp; used to take his devotees for preaching. Sometimes he used to take his jatha ( group of devotees) to Nigaha. In the year 1585, when Bhai ji was going back to his village from Nigaha , he stayed at Amritsar. At Amritsar, in the company of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt;, he learnt about his living , life of Sikhs &amp;amp; preachings of  Satguru which made him stay back at Amritsar. He had not seen such happiness, bloom &amp;amp; recognition in his life. He also asked the Satguru to grant him Sikhism to which &lt;strong&gt;GURU SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt; replied  Purkha, Sikhi utte Sikhi nahin tikdi. He asked him to firstly get rid off all the things which go against Sikhism, only then he will be able to accomplish Sikhism. When you follow AKAL PURAKH&#39;S footsteps &amp;amp; follow the path of truth, you will need to tolerate the anger of common man also. So if you can give such a sacrifice, only then you can go along with Sikhism. Bhai Manj ji came back to his village &amp;amp; first of all destroyed the Peerkhana &amp;amp; stopped praying to Sakhi Sarvar. Fate took such a turn that his cattle started dying but still Bhai Ji remained unshaken, kept working with his full faith in AKAL PURAKH. After that he was taken off from the position of leader of the village due to complaints received from people but he remained steady. Then Bhai Manj Ji came to &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ARJUN DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;amp; indulged himself into serving the Guru Ghar. Like this , he began to earn Sikhism. He took the job of collecting wood for public kitchen. Everyday, after listening to the Guru&#39;s preachings &amp;amp; prayers, he used to go to the jungle to collect wood &amp;amp; while roaming he used to say that need not worry if false money has gone away, I have earned the true money. Bhai Manj Ji used to collect wood from a jungle near Sultan Wind, where the Gurudwara has been built now. Such happened one day that when Bhai Ji was coming back to Amritsar with wood above his head, strong winds struck on the way. Bhai Ji kept walking taking care of the wood, a strong blow of wind struck him &amp;amp; he fell into a well. The well was shallow &amp;amp; the water level was also low. Bhai ji kept the wood above his head to make sure that they don&#39;t get wet. He kept standing in the well the whole night &amp;amp; kept reciting the holy prayers. On the other side, when Guru Ji found that Bhai Manj Ji had not returned last night, he looked for him &amp;amp; found him inside a well. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ARJUN DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; along with his Sikhs ran towards the well &amp;amp; wanted to take Bhai Ji out by throwing a rope to which Bhai Ji replied that they should take out the wood first so that the public kitchen food could be cooked. Then only Bhai Manj Ji was taken out. Just when Bhai Ji was coming out, Guru Ji hugged him &amp;amp; recited &amp;amp; a shlok&lt;/p&gt;

Manj Pyara Guru ko, Guru Manj Pyara ||&lt;BR /&gt;
Manj Guru Bohitha Jug Langanhara||

&lt;BR /&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;GURU SAIHIB told Bhai Manj Ji that he has passed his test &amp;amp; could ask for anything he wishes to which Bhai Ji asked that he should never sway out of Sikhism &amp;amp; that he is able to follow the Sikh way of Life. GURU SAHIB replied that you are already into Sikhism, ask for something else to which Bhai Ji requested GURU SAHIB to never put any Sikh through such tough tests as it is &quot;Kalyug&#39;s&quot; time &amp;amp; Sikhs won&#39;t be able to take such tests. Also don&#39;t take away the public kitchen food to which GURU SAHIB replied that whatever you say would be accomplished &amp;amp; GURU SAHIB sent him to his home in Hoshiarpur to preach Sikhism.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI THADA SAHIB&lt;/b&gt; is situated in Distt City Amritsar.
&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;
This Gurudwara Sahib is situated in the prikarma of GOLDEN TEMPLE SHRI HARIMADIR SAHIB AMRITSAR. Sitting here &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU RAM DAS SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; used to supervise the construction of GURUDWARA SAHIB and excavation of SROVAR SAHIB. Holy Pothy sahibs brought from SHRI GOINDWAL SAHIB were kept here in order to edit SHRI GURU GRANTH SAHIB. Wazir Khan (Governer of Lahore) was cured of disease by performing kar sewa here at instance of Baba Budha Ji. There is a legend that &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; also visited this holy place. Here &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; recited shabad in Rag Ramkali &quot;Athsath tirath jah sadhu pag dareh&quot;. Taking holy dip here one gets blessings equivalent to 68 holy Pilgrimages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI LAKHISAR SAHIB&lt;/b&gt; is situated near Village Lakhi Jungle, Distt Bathinda. Gurudwara Sahib is situated at a distance of 15 Km from Bathinda City and 6 Km from town Goniana Mandi.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/b&gt; :- &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; visited this place and recited Holy &quot;Japji Sahib&quot;. GURU SAHIB blessed this place by saying that whosoever will hear or recite JAPJI SAHIB on Puranmashi (the full moon Day) and take bath in holy sarovar, all his wishes would be fulfilled. This place was dense forest and After GURU SAHIB visit and recitation of Path it was know as Lakhi Jungle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; ;- &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; also visited this place whle going to Lahore from Delhi. .&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU HARRAI SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; :- &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU HARRAI SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; also visited this place during his journeys.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/b&gt; :- &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/b&gt; visited this place and blessed this place as \&quot;Place of liberation\&quot;. GURU SAHIB took the milk of Brown and Black Cow of Bhai Soma Ji and blessed him with milk and son. GURU SAHIB USED datan of Palahi tree and buried that twig at this place, with time which has now become a full fledged tree of Phalahi. A Sarovar of Bhai Bhagtu Ji exists nearby. GURU SAHIB also arranged the third Kavi Darbar at this place.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI DEGSAR SAHIB PAATSHAAHI 6TH &amp;amp; 10TH SAHIB&lt;/b&gt; is situated in the Katana Village In Distt. Ludhiana. GURUDWARA SAHIB is situated on the Doraha Nillon Link Road by the Side of Canal&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;PAATSHAAHI 6TH RELATED: &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; came to this place on 20th Phagun 1675. GURU JI had 7 cannons, 1100 horse riders &amp;amp; Chandu Qaidi ( the one who was involved in SHRI GURU ARJUN DEV JI&#39;s martyrdom), one gown with 52 flower buds with which he freed 52 prisoners from Gwalior fort. He also took rest here for a night &amp;amp; tied his horse with a &quot;Ber&quot; tree. This place is known as DAMDAMA SAHIB.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;PAATSHAAHI 10TH RELATED: &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI &lt;/b&gt;, on becoming &quot;Uchh Da Pir&quot;, came here on 11 Poh 1761 Bikrami. Along with him came Bhai Daya Singh, Bhai Dharam Singh, Bhai Maan Singh, Bhai Nabi Khan &amp;amp; Bhai Gani Khan. He got his bed placed under the &quot;BER SAHIB&quot; &amp;amp; took rest. He also distributed the &quot;DEG&quot; with his holy hands &amp;amp; named this place as &quot;DEGSAR SAHIB&quot;. So whoever offers DEG with a promise, his desire is fulfilled by GURU SAHIB.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;RIVER RELATED: In the year 1854, a survey was conducted regarding Sirhind river &amp;amp; it was proposed to pass a river from this place but the engineer, Mr. Smith, who was taking care of the digging work got blind while cutting the &quot;BERI SAHIB&quot;. Blood came out wherever the &quot;BERI SAHIB&quot; was hit. The foreigner engineer regretted &amp;amp; offered DEG of Rs 51 &amp;amp; he began to see again. Then this place was not touched at all &amp;amp; the river was made to bend &amp;amp; pass.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;b&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI BHATHA SAHIB&lt;/b&gt; is situated in the Ropar City in Distt RoopNagar. Situated on Ropar Chandigarh Main road Gurudwara Sahib is related to tenth Guru &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/b&gt;. GURU SAHIB came here for four times.&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;First time GURU SAHIB here came on the way to Shri Anandpur Sahib after winning the battle of Bhangani via Gurudwara Shri Baoli Sahib Zirakpur and Gurudwara Shri Nadha Sahib Panchkula. At this place was Bhath (Kiln) Which was burning to full capacity. When GURU SAHIB asked a laborer working there for place to stay and rest, he pointed towards hot Brick Klin (Bhatha). As soon as GURU SAHIBS horse&#39;s hoof touched the Bhatha it cooled down. Chaudary Nihang Khan was informed about the incident, when he came there he saw GURU SAHIB Sitting on the klin. Chaudary bowed his head in front of GURU SAHIB and took him to his fort.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Second time GURU SAHIB came to this place for the engagement of Alam Khan, Chaudary Nihang Khans Son.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Third time GURU SAHIB came to this place returning from Kurkshetra.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Fourth and last time GURU SAHIB came to this place after leaving Shri Anandpur Sahib forever.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI KESGARH SAHIB&lt;/b&gt; is situated in the central place of city ANANDPUR SAHIB. It is also known as TAKHT SHRI KESGARH SAHIB. After the establishment of Anandpur Sahib, &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/b&gt; used to hold congregations on this hill. Revelation of Khalsa and first initiation (Khande Di Pahul) took place here. At that time the hill of KESGARH SAHIB was at least 10-15 feat higher than its present height. By the side of this hill there stood another hill. It was known as &quot;Tambu (tent) Wali Pahari&quot; because a special tent was set up here on the day of revelation of Khalsa. This hill does not exist any more. Similarly, there was a long range of small hills extending from Kesgarh Sahib to Anandpur fort.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;KESGARH SAHIB fort was built in 1699. The hill armies attacked Anandpur Sahib several times between 1700 and 1705 but never could the invading armies reach Kesgarh Sahib because it was a very strong fort and before reaching the gates of this fort the armies had to capture the fort at Taragarh, Agamgarh, Fatehgarh and Anandgarh. This could not happen even once in the history of Anandpur Sahib. It was only on December 6,1705, when GURU SAHIB abandoned the town, the hill armies entered this fort and demolished it. The Sikhs could not enter Anandpur Sahib till Baba Banda Singh Bahadur subjugated the ruler of Bilaspur. The Sikhs had to face another wave of persecution after the fall of Baba Banda Singh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Within the next ten years most of the Sikh homeland was under the rule of Maharaja Ranjit Singh, the Sikh Misls and the Patiala dynasty and this meant peace in the Punjab; hence Anandpur Sahib was most safe place for the Sikhs. Takht Shri Keshgarh Sahib is the main shrine at Anandpur Sahib. At Anandpur Sahib there are lying many historical Relics (Pictures in Photo Gallery) which belong to &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/b&gt;, Khanda (Double Edged Sword) GURU JI used to prepare amrit on the revelation of Khalsa Day. Kataar It was &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGHS&lt;/b&gt; personal Dagger he used to carry it with him. Saif It is double edged Weapon presented to GURU SAHIB by Mughal Emperor Bahadur Shah. Gun was presented to GURU SAHIB by one of sikhs from lahore.

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;

&lt;B&gt;GURDWARA SRI SHEESH MAHAL SAHIB&lt;/B&gt; is situated in the Kiratpur Sahib City, Distt Ropar. this is Birth Place of &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU HARRAI SAHIB JI&lt;/B&gt; and &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU HARKARISHAN SAHIB JI&lt;/B&gt;. &lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			&lt;B&gt;SRI GURU HARRAI SAHIB JI&lt;/B&gt; was born to Father Baba Gurditta ji and Mother Mata Nihal ji&lt;BR /&gt;
			&lt;B&gt;SRI GURU HARKARISHAN SAHIB JI&lt;/B&gt; was born to Father &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU HARRAI SAHIB JI&lt;/B&gt; and Mother Mata Krishana ji.

&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI AMB SAHIB&lt;/b&gt; is situated in the Bhairowal Village of Tarn Taran Distt.&lt;br&gt;
SECOND PAATSHAAHI &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Son&#39;s Boon to Bhai Khema Ji - Resident of Village Bhairowal:- &lt;br&gt;
When &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/b&gt; was going from CHAAPRI SAHIB to KHADOOR SAHIB, on the way He took rest at Bhairowal town (Bhairowal Sahib). There were many Sikh followers including BHAI GURDASS JI &amp;amp; BABA BUDDA JI. There was an old Sikh follower whose age was 70 years, Bhai Khema Ji, who used to stay in Village Bhairowal. He had no children. He served GURU SAHIB &amp;amp; his followers with a great zeal. Pleased with his service, GURU SAHIB asked him his wish to which he said that he wanted a son. GURU JI gave a boon to Bhai Khema for a son &amp;amp; respectfully started his journey from Bhairowal to KHADOOR SAHIB. Like this, at the age of 70, the Sikh follower Bhai Khema Ji was blessed with a son as a result of boon given by &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;About &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI &lt;/b&gt;and &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU RAMDAS JI &lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;

&lt;br&gt;When Emperor Akbar came to Lahore, the Khatris and Brahmins complained him that &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU AMARDASS JI&lt;/B&gt; at Goindwal Sahib has started a new religion. He has given up the old scriptures and customs. He doesn&#39;t even know that the great hymn from Hindu scriptures is Gayatri &amp; neither does he recite the same. He has made his own religious scripture and recites only that. He has created a danger to the Hindu religion. On listening to their complaint, Akbar assured them that he will speak to GURU SAHIB and get them justice. After this Akbar sent a message to GURU SAHIB stating that the Khatris and Brahmins are complaining against Him. He should come to Lahore and give an answer to their complaints. On getting Akbar&#39;s message, &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU AMARDASS JI&lt;/B&gt; asked BHAI JETHA JI (&lt;B&gt;SRI GURU RAMDASS JI&lt;/B&gt;) to go to Lahore. On listening GURU SAHIB&#39;s order, BHAI JETHA JI requested that he had not studied any Shastras so how would he give answers to the questions asked in the meeting. GURU SAHIB, with his kindness, said that He need not worry. In the court of the Emperor, whenever someone asks you a question, you start thinking about me and look towards your right arm. You will get the knowledge about all the Vedas and Shastras. You would be able to answer all the questions without any difficulty. After getting GURU SAHIB&#39;s blessings, BHAI JETHA JI started his journey to Lahore. At night, He took rest at his house in Choona Mandi Lahore. Next morning, after offering prayers, he went to the Emperor&#39;s court. In the court, in presence of Akbar, he gave an answer to the complaints of Khatris &amp; brahmins regarding Gayatri, in a very peaceful manner. Before giving an answer to the complaint, BHAI JETHA JI recalled the words told to him by GURU SAHIB &amp; while looking towards his right arm. He recited the Gayatri prayers and then explained its meaning also. After hearing the meanings with vocals, everyone including the complainants were amazed and were not able to ask any further question. listening to meaning filled answer given by BHAI JETHA JI, the Emperor got very happy and pointed the complainants as liers and addressed &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU AMARDASS JI&lt;/B&gt; as heavenly figure. Emperor presented a robe of honor to BHAI JETHA JI before bidding him farewell respectfully. After getting respect from the court, when BHAI JETHA JI was passing through the market, at one of the shop he saw a very beautiful &amp; expensive cloth. He wanted to get a gown for GURU JI from this cloth. But due to shortage of money, BHAI JI couldn&#39;t get it done. On the other hand, &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU AMARDASS JI&lt;/B&gt; while sitting in the royal court at SRI GOINDWAL SAHIB, was moving his arms over his chest in order to remove wrinkles from the gown. When Bhai Ballu Ji inquired about that Maharaj, why are you doing so ? GURU SAHIB replied that BHAI JETHA JI got him a gown sewn from Lahore &amp; he was getting him to wear it..&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The next day when BHAI JETHA JI started from Lahore to Goindwal Sahib, he saw nonseasonal mango&#39;s in the market. Looking at the beauty of nonseasonal mango&#39;s, BHAI JI thought that he should take this beautiful gift for GURU SAHIB. BHAI JI bought a mango for one rupee and started towards Goindwal Sahib. BHAI JETHA JI spent a night on the way, he reached village Bhairowal (Now known as BHAIROWAL SAHIB) near Goindwal Sahib. After taking rest at Bhairowal village, when BHAI JI started his journey again, But he noticed that the juice started flowing from the mangoes. The mangoes might not reach GURU SAHIB. BHAI JETHA JI thought about &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU AMARDASS JI&lt;/B&gt; &amp; said &quot; Hey GOD, this nonseasonal mangoes was bought for you but due to the hot weather, this fruit has started dripping. Kindly accept it and fulfill my desire&quot;. Like this, after offering prayers, BHAI JETHA JI ate the mangoes at Bhairowal only. At the other end, &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU RAMDASS JI&lt;/B&gt; was eating the mangoes and enjoying it at Goindwal Sahib. GURU SAHIB asked Bhai Billu to keep the seed in the window. When BHAI JETHA JI came and told GURU SAHIB about the whole story which happened with Akbar, he was very pleased to know about it. Then GURU SAHIB asked that what had he brought from Lahore city for him to which BHAI JETHA JI replied with folded hands &quot; You are divine, What can I say? I got a beautiful gown stitched for you in my heart only &amp; I also bought a nonseasonal mangoes which started dripping due to heat. I ate it by remembering you at Bhairowal.&quot; GURU SAHIB after listening to this story said that he had eaten the sweet and beautiful fruit that he had brought for him from lahore and has kept the seeds. Then Bhai Ballu Ji brought the seed from the window and showed it to BHAI JETHA JI (&lt;B&gt;SRI GURU RAMDASS JI&lt;/B&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI CHAUBARA SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt; is situated in the Goindwal Sahib City in Tarn Taran Distt. Gurudwara Sahib is situated near to the GURUDWARA SHRI BAOLI SAHIB SHRI GOINDWAL SAHIB. At this place following are the Historical Events had taken place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Residence of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMAR DAS JI&lt;/strong&gt;. Here GURU SAHIB blessed Bibi Bhani ji that GUR GADI will remain in SODHI WANS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;SHRI KILI SAHIB. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMAR DAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; used hold the KILI SAHIB to stand, as GURU SAHIB was of very old Age.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMAR DAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; Blessed &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU RAMDAS JI &lt;/strong&gt;with GURGADI here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Jyoti Jot Asthaan of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU RAMDAS JI.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Birth place of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Tham Sahib, where&lt;strong&gt; SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; used to play in childhood. Also Bibi Bhani ji Used to Prepare Langar here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;PALKI SAHIB of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt;. In this Palki Sahib GURU SAHIB carried SHRI GURU GRANTH SAHIB (COMPILATION OF BANI OF FIRST FOUR GURU SAHIBS) to SHRI HARIMADIR SAHIB.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Sacred Hairs and Chola Sahib of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMAR DAS JI&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; came here to Baba Mohan das to pick SANCHIAA SAHIB.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;GURUDWARA KHOOH &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU RAM DAS JI&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI NANAKMATTA SAHIB&lt;/b&gt; is situated in the Distt, Udham Singh Nagar, UttraKhand. During third Udassi &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/b&gt; sat here under dead and dried Pipal tree. With divine touch of GURU SAHIB pipal tree came to life again. When Sidh\&quot;s saw this, they felt jealous. They used their powers and tried to lift the pipal tree under which GURU SAHIB was sitting out of the ground. When the tree had risen by a few feet, GURU SAHIB simply placed his hand on it and it stopped rising. The same tree can be seen in the GURUDWARA SAHIB premises. The weather being cold, Bhai Mardana asked the sidhs for some fire. However, they refused to help Bhai Mardana. The yogis, instead, taunted him and told him that he should go and ask his GURU SAHIB who was with him. At this, &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/b&gt; looked at a pile of firewood nearby and it instantly ignited. Bhai Mardana was thus able to keep warm and enjoy the fire. Suddenly, the weather changed for the worse and it began to rain. As a result, the fires lit by the yogis were extinguished but the one lit by GURU SAHIB was not affected at all. Then yogis dig a little place and made a child to sit in there and covered it. They asked the Child that when ever they will ask whose land is this, he should reply, Sidhan Di (Yogis). The next morning, they all gathered together and called GURU SAHIB for a religious discussion. Then in the front of GURU SAHIB when they asked two times whose land is this, the Child replied Sidhan Di. But when GURU SAHIB asked whose land is this, There was reply NANAK MATA, NANAK MATA, NANAK MATA, The yogis realized their mistake and fell at the feet of the GURU SAHIB. GURU SAHIB explained to the yogis the path of true meditation and salvation. Later Baba Almast ji was taking Care of This Place. But Again the Gorakh Matts Harrased Baba Almast ji, had thrown him out and captured this place. They renamed it as GorakhMat. Sidhs also Set fire to Pipal Tree. Baba Almast ji send message to &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; at darolli Bhai. On request of Baba Almast ji &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; came to this place and sprinkled some water on pipal tree and made it live again. The pipal tree at some parts can be felt as burnt. Half of the trees leaves are of redish shade and rest of are of Green shade.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;GURUDWARA SAHIB is 45 KM from Rudarpur, 11 KM from SitarGanj. 500 KM from Chandigarh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;a class=&quot;alink &quot; href=&quot;http://www.nanakmattasahib.com&quot; target=&quot;\&amp;quot;_blank\&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Gurdwara Sri NanakMata Sahib WebSite&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI DARBAR SAHIB KHADOOR SAHIB&lt;/strong&gt; is situated in the Khadoor Sahib city in Tarn Taran Distt. The Eight Guru Sahibaans with their visits to this place made this land a Holy place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;

&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: Left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; during his preaching tours, came 5 times to this place. GURU SAHIB used to stay at BIBI BHARAI&#39;s house. During GURU SAHIB&#39;s last tour when BIBI BHARAI requested GURU SAHIB to stay for one more day, GURU SAHIB replied that he would stay for many days &amp;amp; would take rest on this bed only where he was sitting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; sat on the throne at Kartarpur Sahib, Pakistan. When he came back to Khadoor Sahib, As per the instructions of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI,&lt;/strong&gt; he stayed at BIBI BHARAI&#39;s house for 6 months &amp;amp; 6 days &amp;amp; devoted himself to Naam Simran. GURU SAHIB took rest on the same bed regarding which &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; told about. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; spent rest of his life time as a GURU (around 13 years,) here only by serving his followers with Naam Updesh and at last on March 29th 1552 A.D. , GURU SAHIB Left his heavenly abode at this place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; :-In the year 1541, &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; came to &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; and served for around 12 years, with his devotional service, used to fetch a water filled Gaagar early morning from the Beas river Goindwal Sahib, which is around 9 kms away, for GURU SAHIB to take bath. His service was acknowledged &amp;amp; hence he got &quot;Gurta Gaddi&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU RAMDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; while going from Goindwal Sahib to Guru Chakk (Amritsar), visited KHADOOR SAHIB.&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: Left;\&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; while going from Goindwal Sahib to Amritsar, visited KHADOOR SAHIB.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: Left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/strong&gt; after the marriage of his daughter, BIBI VEERO, went to Goindwal Sahib through KHADOOR SAHIB along with his family. Also some scholars of Sikh Panth, after the cremation of BHAI GURDASS JI, spent the afternoon at KHADOOR SAHIB while going to Amritsar.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: Left;\&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU HAR RAI JI&lt;/strong&gt; while going to Goindwal Sahib along with 2200 horse riders, visited KHADOOR SAHIB on the way.&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: Left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU TEG BAHADUR JI&lt;/strong&gt; after acquiring the GURGADDI, in relation to the upkeep of the various places related to the First GURU Sahiban, came to KHADOOR SAHIB.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: Left;&quot;&gt;Religious Scholar BABA BUDDA JI spent around 12 years here. Here only BABA JI applied Tilak to &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; when he took GURGADDI. Great Philosopher BHAI GURDASS JI spent quite a long time here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Here only &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; worked on improvement of Gurmukhi Lippi &amp;amp; wrote the first Punjabi book in remembrance of which GURUDWARA MALL AKHARA has been built. Here only &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; collected information about&#160;&lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt;, from Bhai Bala Ji and got it documented from Bhai Paira Mokha Ji. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; took care of the &quot;Baani&quot;written by &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI &lt;/strong&gt;(writings in Guru Granth the sacred book of the Sikhs) &amp;amp; also wrote his &quot;Baani&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: Left;&quot;&gt;Bhai Bala Ji&#39;s grave is built near GURUDWARA TAPIANA SAHIB.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;GURUDWARA ANGEETHA SAHIB : It is a historical fact that &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; lived at KHADUR SAHIB for a long period. He left for heavenly abode at KHADOOR SAHIB after performing many great religious, social &amp;amp; cultural activities. The place where GURU&#39;S last sacred rites were performed is given the name of ANGITHA SAHIB PAATSHAHI DUSRI. It is a historical fact that the Eight Gurus by their visit to KHADUR SAHIB, made this town of great historical importance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;KILLA SAHIB : This place was house of a weaver which was purchased later on by Guru Sahib. According to the SAKHI, &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt;&#160; brought water for sacred bath of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; for twelve years from the river Beas at Goindwal Sahib. During this service of bringing water, &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt;&#160; fell striking against the peg of the weaver. After hearing the noise of falling of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt;, the weaver said &quot; Who&#39;s there?&quot;. The weaver&#39;s wife replied &quot; Who else might be there. He might be the homeless Amroo&quot; &amp;amp; spoke some objectionable words against &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI. SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; could not tolerate these words &amp;amp; said casually &quot; Mad, you may say whatever you like against me but donot say anything against my GURU SAHIB. The weaver&#39;s wife actually became mad &amp;amp; with the sacred touch of feet of GURU SAHIB, the peg turned green &amp;amp; developed into a full grown &quot;KAREER&quot; tree. With time, the tree lost its life &amp;amp; till now its preserved in a frame for the devotees to pay tributes at this sacred place. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt; was crowned as GURU by BABA BUDDA JI. &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt; gave twelve blessings and ordered ti install the sacred town GOINDWAL SAHIB as a place of service.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;KHOOH (WELL) OF BIBI AMRO JI: This well was got dug by BIBI AMRO JI, daughter of &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI&lt;/strong&gt;, but the water of the well was saline. On the request of the followers of GURU JI, GURU SAHIB provided a log of wood which was thrown into the well &amp;amp; the water became worth drinking. This well is a historical monument.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;GURUDWARA THARAH SAHIB: After bringing water on foot with dedication from river Beas for the sacred bath of GURU SAHIB &amp;amp; after doing other duties assigned by &lt;strong&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI, SHRI GURU AMARDAS JI&lt;/strong&gt;, sitting on this holy place known as THARAH SAHIB, used to worship in spare time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;SIKH AJAIB GHAR( Museum): Historical potraits, manuscripts, sacred orders of GURU&#39;S, historical coins, documents concerning the development of Gurmukhi script &amp;amp; other available material related to GURU SAHIB&#39;s life are kept in this museum.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt; &lt;b&gt;GURDWARA SRI MANJI SAHIB PATSHAHI NAUVIN ATE DASVIN SAHIB&lt;/b&gt;
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			This place is situated in Village Mulowal Distt Sangrur. &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU TEGBAHADUR SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/b&gt; blessed this place by his visit. &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU TEGBAHADUR SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; came here while on malwa tour and rested here. First GURU SAHIB rested on the place where GURDWARA SRI BISTRA SAHIB is situated. When villagers came to know about GURU SAHIB&#39;s visit, they came and paid their obesence. When GURU SAHIB asked for water, villagers told that water from this well is not drinakble as it was Salty here, GURU SAHIB made it sweet GURDWARA SRI MITHA KHOOH SAHIB is situated at that place. GURU SAHIB stayed here for four days.

			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;b&gt;SRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/b&gt; came to alamgir from Machiwara as UCH DA PEER. At Alamgir Bhai Nigahi Singh Ji gave GURU SAHIB a horse. From there GURU SAHIB came to Raikot riding that horse. There GURU SAHIB came to know that Bhai Nigahi Singhs son and sister were killed by Mughals for gifting Horse to GURU SAHIB. Bhai Nigahi Singh escaped and reached Mulowal. To meet Bhai Nigahi Singh GURU SAHIB came here and blessed him that because of you your paternal family is also blessed. GURU SAHIB made a manji with own hands and blessed this place that he will be present here in Month of Poh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI AND BHAI MOHKAM SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; is situated in Beyt Dwarka, Distt Dwarka, Gujarat. This place can be reached by boat from Okha Port which is situated on approx 30km from Distt city Dwarka. This place was house of Bhai Mohkam Singh Ji, Who was one of Five Pyara&#39;s formed by &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; at Sri Anandpur Sahib. Bhai Mohkam Singh Ji was born here to Mother Sambhali Ji and father Bhai Jagjivan Rai in 1663. Along with his parents Bhai Mohkam Chand Ji visited Sri Anandpur Sahib in 1699. When &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; founded the Khalsa, Bhai Mohkam Chand Ji took the nectar from Guru Sahib and became Bhai Mohkam Singh Ji. After that he remained at Sri Anandpur Sahib in the service of GURU SAHIB. In 1705 Bhai Mohkam Singh Ji died in the battle of Chamkaur Sahib with Mughals.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;
			Before that &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/B&gt; visited this place and stayed at Bhai Mohkam Singh Ji&#39;s ancestors house. And this family was &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/B&gt;s followers after that. &lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;
			This place was discovered before 1999, While Sikh&#39;s were celebrating 300 years of Khalsa Sajna. Local Sikhs with help of Gujarat Govt. found this place and later Baba Lakha Singh Ji Kar Sewa wale got this Gurdwara Sahib constructed and are taking care of it now.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI CHARAN KAMAL SAHIB&lt;/B&gt; is situated in Village Naraina, Teh Dudu, Distt Jaipur, Rajasthan.
			&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;
			&lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; came here while travelling from Talwandi Sabo to Nanded Sahib via Sirsa, Nohar, Sahwa etc. At the request of Mahant Jait Ram Ji of Dadu Samparda, he came here with the Sangat and stayed for 13 days. GURU SAHIB bowed his bow to Dadu&#39;s mausoleum. Along with GURU SAHIB, the Sikhs inquired about the fact that according to Gurmat it was not allowed to bow down in front of any Samadh and punished GURU SAHIB for this mistake. GURU SAHIB gladly accepted the Hukam of the Khalsa and by praised that the Khalsa has fulfilled its duty according to Gurmat and has succeeded in this test. Apart from this, GURU SAHIB created a miracle that his falcon, keeping in mind the sentiments of Mahant Jait Ram ji accepted Pearl millet ( bajra ) food. Where as normally Falcon is flesh eater bird.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;

			This episode of history took place at Mahant Jait Ram Ji&#39;s camp, which is a short distance from this place. When the Sikhs tried to build a Gurdwara Sahib here in Naraina, the Government allotted this place to the Sikhs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI BUDHA JHOR SAHIB&lt;/B&gt; is located in Village Dabla (Old Name Dhab Wala ), Teh Raisinghnagar District Sri GangaNagar, Rajasthan.  Zakariya Khan Bahadur of Lahore district had started targeting the Sikhs, forcing the Khalsa to flee from the Punjab to either the hills or the desert. Massa Rangar was tasked with preventing Sikh pilgrims from approaching Amritsar. Massa Rangar took possession of Sri Darbar Sahib, started drinking meat and alcohol, and made prostitute dance in the Darbar Sahib, On the other hand, Baba Budha Singh Ji, the chief of the Budha Dal Misl, was staying at this place, at village Dhab Wala. As the name implies, this place was a reservoir of water in the center of the desert and a mound of about 2000 Acres. Bhai Bakala Ji from Amritsar reached here and told all the news about Sri Darbar Sahib to Baba Baba Budha Singh Ji. Baba Budha Singh challenged his Sikhs to go to Amritsar and take revenge. Accepting this challenge, Bhai Sukha Singh Ji and Bhai Mehtab Singh Ji started their journey towards Amritsar. When they reached Amritsar, got themself dressed like muslims and arrived at the Golden Temple and said that he had come there to pay the revenue. Massa Rangar was drinking alcohol in Sri Darbar Sahib and watching the prostitute dance. They beheaded Massa Rangar, hanging his head on a spear they fled Sri Darbar Sahib. Taking his head, they left for Rajasthan, On the way they stopped near Hanumangarh for the night. There they played khudo khundi (hockey) with Massa Rangar&#39;s head The next morning they reached Dabla and hung his head on a juniper tree Some of those juniper trees are still preserved here today.
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			There are three places with same reference in this village.
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			&lt;B&gt;Jhor Sahib&lt;/B&gt; :- This is a place where actuall water reservoir is. Baba Budha Singh Ji and his men were staying here near water reservoir, Later Bhai Sukha Singh Ji and Bhai Mehtab Singh Ji brought Massa Rangars head here and hanged with Jand tree, part of which is preserved at Nihang Sahib Gurdwara Sahib. This place was water reservoir of nearly 80 Murabas (Approx 2000 acres).
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			&lt;B&gt;Gurdwara Sahib&lt;/B&gt; :- Local Singh Sangat commettee constructed Gurdwara Sahib near the Moderen day Gang Canal in Village Dabla.
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			&lt;B&gt;Nihang Gurdwara Sahib&lt;/B&gt; :- The place where Nihang Singhs were staying after this incidence. Till many untesils are preserved here. Also The part of Jand tree is preserved here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI ADALAT SAHIB&lt;/B&gt; is situated in the Village Khairabad, Amritsar. Now a days it is situated in Holy City, Amritsar. &lt;BR /&gt; &lt;BR /&gt;

&lt;b&gt;History according to History Board in Gurdwara Sahib&lt;/b&gt; :-
This place is blessed with visit of &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/B&gt;. This area was ruled by Mughals and it was reserved as hunting area for Mughal ruler. &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/B&gt; used come here for hunting and use to spent time taking rest. The reason for first battle of Sikh history came into existence here only. In 1629, when GURU SAHIB came here for hunting with Sikhs, Shahjahan was also here for same purpose near Gumtala. Singh&#39;s saw that One Hawk (Baaz) was killing his prey very cruelty. And this Hawk (Baaz) was of King Shahjahan. Singhs sent there own Hawk and captured the royal Hawk. When royal army of Shahjahan came to know about this incident they tried to threat sikhs and asked for royal hawk. But singhs denied to give it. Royal army warned them of Battle but Sikhs replied &quot;Tusi Baaz Di gal Karde ho asi tuhade Taaz nu Hath Pawange&quot;. Royal army went back and explained the whole story to ShahJahan. In result of this Shahjahan sent Royal army under the command of Mukhalas Khan. And first battle of Sikh history was fought at PIPLI SAHIB where Mukhalas Khan was killed. &lt;BR /&gt; &lt;BR /&gt;
			&lt;B&gt;According to Bhai Kahn Singh Ji Nabha&lt;/B&gt; :-
			The sangat who came with dasvand from Kabul were robbed by thieves and their child was killed. When &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/B&gt; received the news of Amritsar, he came here and revived the boy and punished the thieves.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI DAMDAMA SAHIB&lt;/b&gt;
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			This city is blessed with sacred visit of &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt;. In 1687 during monsoon days, &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; crossing beas camped here while coming from kartapur sahib. Earlier this place was inhabited by &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI&lt;/b&gt; in 1644, but later it was occupied by Chandu Shah and Bhagwan Das Khatri. &lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;

When &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB&lt;/b&gt; camped at place where Gurdwara Shri Granthian Sahib is situated, Bhagwan Das opposed GURU SAHIB and spoke bad words. Due to which the Sikhs taking permission from GURU SAHIB, thrashed him and threw in the river. After hearing the news of his father, Gherd&#39;s son Ratan Chand and Chandu&#39;s son Karam Chand complained to Sube Abdul Khan of Jalandhar. Accepting their request, Abdul Khan attacked GURU SAHIB with an army of 15,000. There was a terrible war in this area for three days, In which Abdul Khan and his son Nabi Bakhsh and five generals were killed. GURU SAHIB came here, opened his waist and took rest. Since then the name of this place came to be Damdama Sahib. Bhai Jattu ji Bhai Mathra ji Bhai Nano ji Bhai Shaktu ji, Sikhs of GURU SAHIB were martyred in this war. GURU SAHIB himself performed the last rites of martyred Sikhs, and also buried the Turks by digging a pit and built a beautiful platform on it. Sitting on that platform, GURU SAHIB organized the diwan and asked that if any Sikh could recite Japuji Sahib, with all pronunciations. Bhai Gopal ji started reciting the pure text of Japuji Sahib. As paath was about to end. GURU SAHIB was thinking, what reward should i give to Sikh who recited so pure Paath and that too with such devotion? While thinking, a thought came to the mind of GURU SAHIB, that i will bless this Sikh with Guru Gaddi.&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			On the other hand, Bhai Sahib thought that if GURU SAHIB is happy, then he should bless him with his horse. At the end of the paath, GURU SAHIB said that Bhai Gopal ji, would have blessed you with Gurtagaddi if the thought of horse hadn&#39;t come to your mind. But still you will be free from cycle births and deaths. In this way, GURU SAHIB told the Sikhs the importance of reciting pure Bani. Even today, those Sikhs who pray at this place assuming GURU SAHIB in person, get their wishes fulfilled. At this place, GURU SAHIB had a story from Pandit Nita Nand ji and cleared the doubts of the mind. Nita Nanda adopted the Sikhi. It was here that GURU SAHIB gave a sermon to Jani Shah Ji and he also received Sikhi Dharan. It is from here that GURU SAHIB sent Bhai Garia ji and other Sikhs for preaching. GURU SAHIB built a beautiful city here. In the city, got Maseet, Dharamshala, Langar built along with 40 wells. Baba Budha Ji and Bhai Gurdas Ji came here to see GURU SAHIB. After GURU SAHIB&#39;s name this city was named Hargobindpur It is from here that Baba Budha ji went to Ramdas in his last days.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI CHOLA SAHIB&lt;/B&gt;
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			When &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/B&gt; went to the Arabian country in 1519 AD during the fourth Udhasi, the Lajward king of the Arab country was informed that there is a Hindu fakir who is preaching in our area, The Lajward king sent GURU SAHIB an invitation to his court. The king had a magical chola, which by wearing would lead to religious conversion. The wearer used to adopt the Muslim religion. After hearing GURU SAHIB teachings, the king thought that if this magical robe is given to him, then the Hindu fakir will preach for our Muslim religion, which will be very beneficial for our religion. The king gave robe to &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/b&gt;. GURU SAHIB ji said that if you want to give the robe, then you should yourself put it on me. After hearing this, the king did not delayed and ordered the officer to help GURU SAHIB to wear this. As there was no bad effect of the robe on GURU SAHIB, Then after some time, Lajvard king said that you should take it off, then GURU SAHIB said, you have put it on me, now you should take it off. Lajvard king again ordered the officer to take off the robe. When the officer started to remove this robe, it became part of the body of &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/B&gt; and stuck to the body. The king was surprised and ordered the officer to remove it with his own strength. Torture GURU SAHIB and he will remove himself. GURU SAHIB Ji was tortured but there was no effect on GURU SAHIB. After seeing GURU SAHIB, the king had to fall on GURU SAHIB&#39;s feet. &lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			GURU SAHIB finished the fourth Udasi, and reached Sri Kartar Sahib( Dera Baba Nanak ) and took off the Udasi bana and put on worldly clothes, then gave Udasi Libas i.e. Chola Sahib to &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU ANGAD DEV JI &lt;/b&gt;as well as Guru Gaddi. Presented on time to time, In the same way, Chola Sahib continued to be passed on along with Guru Gaddi till Panj Patshahiya &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI &lt;/b&gt; In 1604 AD, a Sikh Bhai Tota Ram from Balkh Bukhara (Afghanistan) was serving in the construction of Sarovar of Sri Harmandir Sahib Ji. Tota Ram got hit by spade on his foot while serving, but he did not stopped serving. GURU SAHIB ji called Tota Ram and said, Bhai Sikh, your service is accepted, ask for something from the Guru&#39;s house, Bhai Tota Ram said, You have given me a lot of grace, daughters, sons, happiness, marriage, wealth, but my area is devoid of Sikhism. &lt;b&gt;SHRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI&lt;/b&gt; gave Sri Chola Sahib to Bhai Tota Ram ji and he took it to his city and continued to serve during his lifetime. Tota Ram ji, in his last days, kept this robe in a cave and placed a stone in front of it and prayed, Maharaj, whomever you order, will take robe from here. After a long time, the 9th generation of &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/B&gt; Baba Kabli Mall ji took the devotees of his area to that place. They brought back Chola Sahib and today &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU NANAK DEV JI&lt;/B&gt; 17th descendants of Baba Jagdeep Singh Bedi are serving this Gurdwara Sri Chola Sahib at Dera Baba Nanak, District Gurdaspur Punjab.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;  GURUDWARA SHRI AKALGARH SAHIB &lt;/B&gt;
&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			This village Haripura is situated on little side from Abhohar Gangannagar road. &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; came here from Village Theri Sahib. GURU SAHIB organised a diwan and next day after visiting Village Gurdwara Sahib went back to Village Theri.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI SHINI SAHIB PATSHAHI CHEVIN, MEHAR SINGH WALA&lt;/B&gt;
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			When &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/B&gt; was staying at Daroli Bhai Ki, Sangat from this area requested GURU SAHIB that a lion disturbs them a lot. Listening to villagers request GURU SAHIB came and camped at village Thatha. From that place GURU SAHIB sent five singhs to kill Lion. But Two singhs got killed by attack of Lion. Rest of the singhs came back and told GURU SAHIB about this. Finally GURU SAHIB himself came here and killed the lion at village here. And asked lioness to leave this area. From here GURU SAHIB went back to Village Thatha.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GURUDWARA SHRI PATSHAHI CHEVIN SAHIB&lt;/B&gt;
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			When &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU HARGOBIND SAHIB JI&lt;/B&gt; was staying at Daroli Bhai Ki, A fakir from this village Sunher visited bhai ki daroli three times to have glimpse of GURU SAHIB. But each time he was not able to see GURU SAHIB. But there was wish that if he could see GURU SAHIB. Understanding his position and his desire GURU SAHIB came here to meet fakir. Up on meeting GURU SAHIB he said i had gone three times to see you, but was not able to meet you, Now i request you that you may come here three times to fulfill my wish. So fulfilling fakirs wish GURU SAHIB came here three times. Then GURU SAHIB asked his wish, Fakir told GURU SAHIB that he&#39;s too old now and want to be free from life. SO GURU SAHIB blessed him. This village was populated later on, In those days it was dense jungle here. GURU SAHIB also blessed this place that who so ever comes here his wishes will be fulfilled.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt; GURUDWARA SHRI PATSHAHI DASVIN,&lt;/B&gt;
&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			 After leaving Sri Anandpur Sahib &lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; reached here via Chamkaur Sahib, Machiwara, Alamgir, Dina etc. This place was outer of Fort of Chaudhary Kapura. GURU SAHIB camped here near small pond. When Chaudhary came to know about GURU SAHIB he came here and bowed in front of GURU SAHIB. When GURU SAHIB asked Chaudhary for his fort to fight against Muslims. Chaudhary got scared of Muslims and said no to GURU SAHIB. Then GURU SAHIB left this place and went to village Dhilwan Kalan.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt; GURUDWARA SHRI CHULHA SAHIB,&lt;/B&gt;
&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			 When SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI camped at place where GURDWARA SRI PATSHAHI DASVIN SAHIB is situated in Kotkapura city. Singhs along with GURU SAHIB prepared langar here. GURU SAHIB served langar to the Singhs and the Sangat and he also received langar here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt; GURDWARA SRI GODAVARISAR SAHIB,&lt;/B&gt;
&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			 After leaving Sri Ananpur Sahib &lt;B&gt;SRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; reached here via Chamkaur Sahib, Machiwara, Alamgir, Dina, Kotkapura etc. GURU SAHIB reached here tied his horse with Beri Tree (Jujube Tree) and rested near small pond. When Sodhi Kaul ji came to know about GURU SAHIB&#39;s visit, He came here paid obeisance and had discussions with GURU SAHIB. Later he and his family got baptised here. They presented GURU SAHIB new clothes, GURU SAHIB accepted them and when after changing the clothes GURU SAHIB was about to burn the old clothes, Bhai Kaul Ji requested for old clothes so that they can keep them as gift from GURU SAHIB. GURU SAHIB gave them the old clothes which are still preserved at their residence, in the village. &lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			 Secondly when GURU SAHIB was about to burn the blue robe he was wearing, Bhai Maan Singh requested for the part of that clothe. GURU SAHIB torn of the blue robe and gave him, Bhai Maan Singh Ji put it on his turban. From here onwards the tradition of farla started.&lt;p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;Gurudwara Shri Gupatsar Sahib&lt;/B&gt;
&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			&lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; came here while travelling from Mukatsar Sahib to Talwandi Sabo. Here GURU SAHIB came from Pakka Kalan and stopped here near a pipal tree and well. GURU SAHIB rested here in the afternoon and soon Local Chaudhary Bhai Dal Singh ji came to know about GURU SAHIB&#39;s arrival. He came here and escorted GURU SAHIB towards talwandi sabo. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;Gurudwara Shri Rohila Sahib, Jangirana&lt;/B&gt;
&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			&lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; came here while travelling from Mukatsar Sahib to Talwandi Sabo. GURU SAHIB came here from Gidderbaha and stopped near water and Jand tree. There is a sarovar named tilak rao after a martyr of this village. At this place a person named rohila got martyred. GURU SAHIB sent his sikhs in search of water and they found in village Bambiha. GURU SAHIB camped at that place in night and used to come here in day. He stayed here on both places for 9 days. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;Gurudwara Shri Udeeksar Sahib, Bambiha&lt;/B&gt;
&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			&lt;B&gt;SHRI GURU GOBIND SINGH JI&lt;/B&gt; came to place where Gurdwara Sri Rohila Sahib, Jangirana is situated, while travelling from Mukatsar Sahib to Talwandi Sabo. GURU SAHIB came to this area from Gidderbaha and stopped near water and Jand tree. At that place a person named rohila got martyred. GURU SAHIB sent his sikhs in search of water and they found here in village Bambiha. GURU SAHIB camped at this place in night and used spend the day time there. At this place sangat separated from Sri Anandpur Sahib came and met GURU SAHIB. GURU SAHIB said i had been waiting for you. Here GURU SAHIB baptised 500 Sikhs. He stayed here on both places for 9 days. From here onwards GURU SAHIB went towards Bajak.&lt;/p&quot;&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;   GURDWARA SRI MITHA KHOOH SAHIB, MULOWAL&lt;/b&gt;
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			This place is situated in Village MULOWAL, Distt Sangrur. &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU TEGBAHADUR SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; came here while on malwa tour and rested here. First GURU SAHIB rested on the place where GURDWARA SRI BISTRA SAHIB is situated. When villagers came to know about GURU SAHIB&#39;s visit, they came and paid their obeisance. When GURU SAHIB asked for water, villagers told that water from this well is not drinkable as it was Salty here, GURU SAHIB made it sweet Later GURU SAHIB rested at place which is situated outside the village now. GURU SAHIB stayed here for four days.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;   GURDWARA SRI BISTRA SAHIB, MULOWAL&lt;/b&gt;
			&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;
			This place is situated in Village MULOWAL, Distt Sangrur. &lt;b&gt;SRI GURU TEGBAHADUR SAHIB JI&lt;/b&gt; came here while on malwa tour and rested here. First GURU SAHIB rested here at GURDWARA SRI BISTRA SAHIB. When villagers came to know about GURU SAHIB&#39;s visit, they came and paid their obeisance. When GURU SAHIB asked for water, villagers told that water from this well is not drinkable as it was Salty here, GURU SAHIB made it sweet. GURDWARA SHRI MITHA KHOOH SAHIB is situated there. Later GURU SAHIB rested at place which is situated outside the village now. &lt;BR /&gt;&lt;BR /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
